    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d499">

                <pb facs="0628" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4e 1/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schurmcm</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-18T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                                1924—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>55. Your No. 77 March 13, 4 p.m. and Evans’ telegram to Buforcom March 15.<anchor
                        n="32" xml:id="d499-f1"/> Pending the receipt of further instructions, you
                    should not take such a part in conference with your colleagues as to indicate or
                    commit in any way the position of this Government with respect to the proposal
                    for a preliminary conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d499-f1" n="32" xml:id="d499-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram from Mr. Arthur H. Evans, assistant commercial attaché at Peking, to the
                    Bureau of Foreign and Domestic Commerce; not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
